# No Demo / Sample Framing

HelpNova is **not** presented as a demo website, sample project, or unfinished concept in anything a visitor can read.

When writing or editing public UI copy (headings, body, badges, notices, empty states, metadata, legal heroes, CTAs), if you see framing like **demo**, **sample**, **concept website**, **draft policy**, **illustrative only**, **local simulation**, **not a live service**, or similar, **remove or rewrite it**. Do not leave empty badges, empty notice cards, or orphaned disclaimer boxes.

## Prefer

- Confident product language: how HelpNova handles privacy, support, automation, and inbox workflows.
- Clear, useful explanations without apologizing for “not being real.”

## Avoid in visitor-facing text

- demo, sample, preset, mock, placeholder, dummy
- concept website, draft notice, editable sample, demonstration-only
- “not a finalized policy,” “not an operational service,” “interactive demonstrations” as product identity

## Keep

- Code, types, file names, routes (e.g. `/demo`), and internal comments may still use technical names.
- Do not invent fake claims (sent messages, created accounts, connected integrations, live AI answers, testimonials, measured outcomes).

## Example

❌ `HelpNova is currently a concept website with interactive demonstrations. This privacy notice is a draft…`

✅ Remove the disclaimer card entirely, or replace nearby copy with direct product privacy language only.
